  "problem": "Use the first three terms of the binomial expansion of $(4+x)^{5}$ in ascending powers of $x$ to approximate $(3.89)^{5}.$ Give your answer to three decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "The binomial theorem for positive integer $n$ states that\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+\u2026+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $a=4,$ $b=x,$ and $n=5,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(4+x)}^{5} & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{0}){(4)}^{5}{(x)}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{1}){(4)}^{5-1}{(x)}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{5}{2}){(4)}^{5-2}{(x)}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1{(4)}^{5}+5{(4)}^{4}{(x)}^{1}+10{(4)}^{3}{(x)}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1\\,024+5(256)(x)+10(64)({x}^{2})+\u22ef \\\\  & =1\\,024+1\\,280x+640{x}^{2}+\u22ef\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(4+x)}^{5}\u22481\\,024+1\\,280x+640{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-0.11$ into the above approximation of $(4+x)^{5}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3.89)^{5} & =(4+(-0.11))^{5} \\\\  & \u22481\\,024+1\\,280(-0.11)+640(-0.11)^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,024-1\\,280(0.11)+640(0.012\\,1) \\\\  & =1\\,024-140.8+7.744 \\\\  & =890.944,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places.",
